  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0916">Theorem <span data-tag="0916">5.2.9.1</span>.</a>$\infty $-category!oppositeopposite!$\infty $-category Let $\calE $ denote the full subcategory of $\Fun ( \Cat _{\infty }, \Cat _{\infty })$ spanned by the equivalences. Then $\calE $ is equivalent to the $($nerve of the$)$ discrete category $\{  \id , r \} $, where $r: \Cat _{\infty } \rightarrow \Cat _{\infty }$ is a functor which associates to every $\infty $-category its opposite. </p>
